/target

# The shipped downloads. They are distributed as GitHub release assets --
# latest.json points installed copies at those URLs -- so they are built here
# and uploaded to the release, never committed: a 20 MB binary per release
# turned the history into half a gigabyte of the same file over again.
bubbleTranslate.dmg
bubbleTranslate.exe
bubbleTranslate-linux-x86_64

# The zipped Windows download. Browsers show "isn't commonly downloaded" on a
# bare unsigned .exe and discard it unless the warning is clicked through; the
# same bytes inside a zip arrive without it. Built and uploaded like the rest.
bubbleTranslate-windows-x64.zip

# Source artwork and exported marks, kept on this machine rather than in the
# repository. The icons that actually ship (linux/*.svg, windows/*.ico) are
# tracked by name where they live.
logos/

# The last unlimited builds, kept on this machine only. Never published:
# the download on GitHub is the metered build, under the plain name.
bubbleTranslate-free*

# Where those builds are kept. The rule above already covers them by name;
# this covers the shelf itself, so anything else set aside here is out of the
# repository by virtue of where it was put rather than what it was called.
/backup/

# The bundle the DMG is built around. The DMG is the download and carries the
# same app inside it, so tracking both would put fifteen megabytes of the same
# binary in every release commit.
bubbleTranslate.app/

# What windows\make-icon.ps1 leaves behind for eyeballing the mark. The .ico it
# writes beside them is the one that ships, and that one is tracked.
windows/preview-*.png

# The previous download, moved aside because it was running when release.ps1
# rebuilt it. The next release deletes it; it is history's copy either way.
bubbleTranslate.exe.locked-old

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets, never committed. Real credentials live outside the repo entirely --
# the service reads them from `wrangler secret`, the signing key from a
# keychain -- but this is the net that catches a stray one before it ships.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
# The service's local dev secrets (also covered by service/.gitignore).
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Checksums of the shipped downloads. Generated per release and uploaded to the
# GitHub release beside the binaries they describe, not tracked -- the binaries
# themselves are release assets too.
SHA256SUMS.txt

# The App Store build: the provisioning profile is per account, the package is output.
appstore/embedded.provisionprofile
bubbleTranslate-appstore.pkg
